# Normalise text to LF in the repository and check it out in the platform's own
# style. This says in the REPO what core.autocrlf was only saying on one machine:
# the setting that made this work here came from Git for Windows' system config,
# so a reinstall with different setup options would have changed it silently and
# for every repo at once. Verified a no-op when added on 2026-09-07 -- all 348
# tracked files were already LF in the index, so nothing renormalised.
* text=auto

# The TRX fixtures are parsed by XmlDocument, which preserves a CR inside text content, and
# the goldens were recorded from an LF working tree. A CRLF checkout (autocrlf on a fresh
# clone) makes TheTestRunMatchesTheRecordedAnswer fail on \r\n vs \n in the failure message
# -- an environmental red that looks like a parity break. Pin them so every checkout parses
# to the recorded answer. This rule is LAST because later rules win: it has to override the
# blanket text=auto above.
tests/Janet.Tests/Fixtures/**/*.trx text eol=lf
